the expanse is a sci-fi show based on a  series of books it's got drama politics  mysteries space battles space lasagna  and the later seasons get really wild  the expanse is set in a future where  humans have colonized the solar system  earth is the old superpower  overpopulated and in decline Mars is an  independent world with strong science  and military working to terraform Mars  to transform the Red Rock into a garden  the people of the asteroid belt are  called belters they live dangerous lives  on the frontiers of space and have their  own culture and language at the start of  the story scientists find a mysterious  alien virus called the proto molecule  Earth Mars and the belt get into  conflict trying to control it and in the  first three seasons the heroes of the  story managed to end this war but the  proto molecule grows into the ring a  kind of wormhole connecting to thousands  of new habitable worlds so who are the  main characters facing this new frontier  in season four Holden is a brave heroic  leader he was born on earth to a family  of eight parents five fathers and three  mothers who all contributed to Holden's  DNA they ran a farm in Montana and  raised Holden to stand up for truth and  justice he served in the earth space  Navy but quit when he was ordered to  fire on civilians so at the start of the  story  Holden's on a ship called the Canterbury  until it's suddenly destroyed as part of  a proto molecule conspiracy so Holden  steps up as a leader and fights to  protect his crew Alex amos and naomi the  dangers they face bring them together as  an unlikely family on a ship called the  Ross and ante Holden can be naive and  impulsive so Naomi challenges him to  make smarter decisions they start a  relationship bonding over their shared  determination to do what's right the  crew investigate the proto molecule and  Holden meets detective Miller Miller is  cynical and brutal which challenges  Holden's heroic ideals Miller shows that  to get [ __ ] done  sometimes you got to be morally flexible  so sometimes Holden does bad things for  the greater good even killing innocent  people to save others but Naomi reminds  Holden of his humanity and helps him to  stay grounded  Holden struggles with being a leader and  being a hero but when push comes to  shove he's always willing to risk his  life to save others in season 2 miller  dies crashing into venus with a moon  full of proto molecule but in season 3  Holden has visions of Miller the proto  molecule uses Miller's consciousness as  a tool to communicate with Holden the  alien intelligence behind the molecule  guide told him to open the ring gates  so now Holden and his crew face the  mystery and danger of alien worlds naomi  is a smart skilled engineer she is a  belter with a secret past  she was once involved with a radical  faction of the OPA a group fighting for  belter rights she had a son with an OPA  guy but the father took the baby away  from her and Naomi was on a mission  where innocent people died so Naomi is  haunted with trauma and guilt she found  support on the cat with Amos Amos is  strange  he's unemotional and violent but Naomi  helps Amos to make moral decisions and  Amos reassures Naomi that she's a good  person no matter what happened in her  past in the conflict over the proto  molecule it's the belters who suffer  most which reminds Naomi of her loyalty  to her people so against the wishes of  Holden and the crew Naomi gives a proto  molecule sample to the OPA and she  leaves the Rosi to join a belter ship  Holden and Amos feel betrayed but Naomi  believes in the belt and in their  mission to build an independent belter  nation naomi is close friends with OPA  leader drummer and helps her out in  season 3 but in the end Naomi returns to  the Rawson onte and to Holden Amos and  Alex because while the belters are her  people the Rosi crew are  family and her home Amos is a mechanic  born on earth he's tough blunt and  emotionally detached  he's secretive about his past but it's  implied that he was sexually exploited  as a child as part of organized crime in  Baltimore he learned to suppress all  emotion and do whatever's necessary to  survive he uses brutal violence with no  hesitation or remorse sometimes he gets  in fights with his friends like Alex he  knows he's not good at making the right  choices so that's why he's so reliant on  Naomi she's his guide star lighting the  way through the dark so when Naomi  leaves the Rosi Amos is forced to think  for himself some more he makes new  friendships with Anna and prax cos  despite all the darkness in Amos he's a  funny and lovable guy fans call him  murder snuggles cuz he's affectionate  and honest and loyal and vulnerable and  he's trying so hard to be a better man  alex is a cheerful Martian pilot with a  Texan accent and a fondness for country  music he flew with a Martian Navy and  discovered his passion for spaceflight  he has a wife and child on Mars but he's  left them behind because he believes his  true purpose is to fly with the rawson  Dante doing good and saving lives  Holden Naomi and Amos are Alex's family  now but there is a sadness to Alex that  he's estranged from his wife and child  he finds comfort in a friendship with  Bobby Martian Marine Alex's expertise as  a pilot saves the Rocinante countless  times so the main heroes of the story of  the Rosi crew Holden Naomi Amos and Alex  on earth there's other Sarala a powerful  politician in the United Nations which  controls earth of a Sarala is charming  and scheming and sassy as all [ __ ] in  season one she's ruthless in defending  Earth's power she tortures and  blackmails and betrays a friend because  years ago Avasarala son was killed by  the OPA and she's determined to protect  her  remaining family she believes earth  comes first and she'll do anything to  defend her home but other Sarala  uncovers corruption within her own  government her colleague Aaron Wright  conspires to weaponize the proto  molecule so other Sarala works with the  Rosi crew and with belters and martians  and risks her own life to stop Aaron  right and prevent war Avasarala learns  to see the humanity in all people in  belters and Martians as well as earthers  in season 3 she becomes  secretary-general the most powerful  person on earth and she urges peace and  unity as humanity faces new worlds  beyond the ring Bobby is a Martian  Marine a tough and confident warrior she  comes from a military family and was  fiercely loyal to Mars at the start of  season 2 she couldn't wait for a war to  wipe out earth but on Ganymede her squad  is killed by a proto molecule creature  and Bobby discovers that her own Martian  government unleashed this monster to  test it as a weapon  so Bobby rebels against Mars and brings  the truth to other Sarala  Bobby helps the earth government that  she had once hoped to destroy and fights  for the greater good in season three she  rejoins the Martians but then she turns  against them to help hold him Bobby is a  Martian and a soldier and she wants to  fight for good but she says the hardest  part of this game is figuring out who  the enemy really is drama is a leader of  the OPA fighting for a future for  belters she is proud uncompromising  fiercely loyal to the belt and also  pretty good at space handball in season  three she becomes the captain of the  behemoth the massive OPA ship drummers  legs are crushed in an accident so Naomi  sets up a mech so that she can walk  drummer and Naomi's friendship runs deep  and it's tied to their identities as  belters so by the end of season 3 Earth  Mars and the belt are at a delicate pace  but the new worlds beyond the ring gate  promise more conflict and more mystery  what alien race made the gates and what  happened to them what new dangers will  Naomi Alex and Amos face how will the  ring effect of a Cyril on earth Bobby on  Mars and drummer in the OPA is peace and  humanity possible in the col